      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary angiography and the assessment of blood lipoproteins were carried out in 43 patients with recent (not more than three months old) angina. A rise in cholesterol above 270 mg/dl and/or triglycerides above 200 mg/dl was demonstrated in 19. The level of alpha-cholesterol was below 35 mg/dl in 11 of 24 normolipidemic patients. The apoprotein B/apoprotein AI ratio was above 1.0 in 7 of 13 patients with normal cholesterol levels. Plasma phospholipid composition was disturbed in 4 of 6 patients with normal apoprotein B/apoprotein AI rations. Therefore, atherogenic changes in plasma lipoprotein composition were found in 95% of patients with recent angina."},
